Current Approach:

Computing temporal derivatives (rate of change) of neural activity
Apply PCA to these derivatives across neurons
Extracting rich statistical features (mean, std, FFT) from each PC timecourse
Training a logistic regression classifer on these features

Pros:
- Temporal dynamics captured
- Dimensionality reduction
- Rich feature set
- Balanced class handeling

Cons:
- Low Variance Explained (27%): most information is in high frequency noise or single neuron idiosyncrasies, are derivatives the right choice?
- Bad classification on naturalistic videos

Missing:
- trial to trial variability
- neuron selectivity
- spatial patterns
- timing precision


